{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787175153877908001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"stuckup-trophic-nabarlek","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"1ecb618374d87e5562ef78a112e938a0070ed71484b5018876b660b970e2d468","event_uuid":"73e16b6e-813c-471a-aa24-a497af521667","position":{"commit_sha":"2269bcc93a1b5f56d1fecd9993b685e33c6b0807","position":"1787172698189640001-73e16b6e-813c-471a-aa24-a497af521667"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ec444e4528656e3d9ed6493e666acbdde87709ccefa0dd1ffd31a29e14d6463c","event_uuid":"8eea48ec-c464-4fbf-beaf-7198f4d3dc6a","position":{"commit_sha":"321bb1ca28032438301cd30787a2e5a171b14cce","position":"1787172710425116001-8eea48ec-c464-4fbf-beaf-7198f4d3dc6a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f18866e3adf8d8d3c656cf16c857b349ff2d5e2aa5b7950fa7c2283fd7a9fbfe","event_uuid":"bf38936b-8e12-407d-b9c3-3945b6c40bf2","position":{"commit_sha":"1b6e09ab53f1f9591c3b6f06eec58d7965795b56","position":"1787172715835169001-bf38936b-8e12-407d-b9c3-3945b6c40bf2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787172698189640001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"bf38936b-8e12-407d-b9c3-3945b6c40bf2","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"afa0-2e15-7db8-4d5b"}],"description":"## Context\nFault-seeding under afa0-2e15 (rival-ammoniacal-crustacean) proved a real detection gap in\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_reads_under_sync_contention.py`.\n\n`_assert_complete_or_loud` stops at `isinstance(doc, expected_shape)`. Two seeded faults —\nF3 (`show` emits `{}`, exit 0) and F6 (`show` emits a record with `ticket_id` removed,\nexit 0) — passed BOTH generic tests while the original regression\n`test_cli_show_complete_or_erroring_under_write_burst` went RED on each.\n\nSo the generic property currently certifies a read as \"COMPLETE-or-LOUD\" when the payload is\nshape-valid but content-hollow. The gap applies to all four surfaces (show/list/search/ready),\nnot just show — nothing in the property asserts that a returned record carries identity.\n\nNote: this is a gap against the property's INTENT, not against its docstring (which promises\nshape only). Closing it is a deliberate strengthening, not a bug fix.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a per-surface content-completeness predicate to the SURFACES table (e.g. show -> the\n  object carries a truthy `ticket_id`; list/ready/search -> every element that is present\n  carries one, with valid-empty `[]` still passing).\n- Prove RED first by re-applying seeds F3 and F6 from afa0-2e15 (`/tmp/faultseed/seeds.py`,\n  recorded in that ticket's matrix comment), then GREEN on the restored tree.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n- With F3 seeded, both generic tests must go RED (they currently pass).\n- With F6 seeded, both generic tests must go RED (they currently pass).\n- Unseeded tree: `pytest tests/interfaces/store/` GREEN.\n- `make lint`, `make typecheck`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Seeded fault F3 is detected by the generic property.\n- [ ] Seeded fault F6 is detected by the generic property.\n- [ ] Valid-empty results (`[]`) still pass, remaining distinguishable from truncated output.\n- [ ] No increase in the property's wall-clock runtime.\n- [ ] The original regression test is left unchanged by this ticket.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_reads_under_sync_contention.py","reason":"Add per-surface content-completeness predicate to close the proven F3/F6 gap."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["ci","test-quality","concurrency"],"ticket_id":"8469-85a7-88b7-4bbb","ticket_type":"task","title":"Generic reads-under-contention property accepts partial-success payloads on all four surfaces","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["73e16b6e-813c-471a-aa24-a497af521667","8eea48ec-c464-4fbf-beaf-7198f4d3dc6a","bf38936b-8e12-407d-b9c3-3945b6c40bf2"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787175153877908001,"uuid":"ca3cbd8c-2391-4e5f-8959-5123063e45f9"}